{"flow":{"nodes":[{"width":282,"height":388,"id":"comment-b2b3e929-625e-4292-b583-059565b0f5fd","type":"comment","data":{"title":"Read me first","text":"Twelve multi-step word problems, each asked twice: once with the model's reasoning off, and once with it on at medium effort.\n\nThe prompt asks for only the final number. With reasoning off, a model has to answer without working anything out. With it on, it can think first, out of sight.\n\nFollow the wires: Table and Text Fields, Prompt, JavaScript Evaluator, Vis."},"position":{"x":-1200,"y":-640},"positionAbsolute":{"x":-1200,"y":-640},"dragHandle":".node-header"},{"width":422,"height":446,"id":"table-43d251c4-8bc3-47a8-b9df-fdc00373bd88","type":"table","data":{"title":"Word problems","columns":[{"header":"Question","key":"question"},{"header":"Expected","key":"answer"}],"rows":[{"__uid":"2c4465e9-5869-40c4-ae94-681ace3a781c","question":"A train leaves at 9:47 AM. It travels 315 km at an average speed of 84 km/h, stops for 23 minutes, then travels another 145 km at 116 km/h. How many minutes after 9:47 AM does it arrive?","answer":"323"},{"__uid":"a1ef7164-6202-4326-bddf-b325b0b38f8d","question":"Maya puts $2,400 in an account that earns 5% interest compounded once a year. At the end of each year, after the interest is paid, she deposits another $300. How many dollars are in the account after 3 years, rounded to the nearest dollar?","answer":"3724"},{"__uid":"eff28469-b46c-465d-8e23-05a6a590cee7","question":"A rectangular garden measures 23 m by 17 m. A path 1.5 m wide runs all the way around the outside of the garden. What is the area of the path, in square meters?","answer":"129"},{"__uid":"e5e40b20-c14b-487a-a199-e4f28b669971","question":"In a class, the ratio of students who walk to school to students who take the bus is 5:7. After 6 walkers switch to taking the bus, the ratio becomes 1:2. How many students are in the class?","answer":"72"},{"__uid":"a21c8175-885f-4007-8ec7-7664b7d4b362","question":"What is the sum of all positive integers less than 200 that are divisible by 6 or by 15, but not by both?","answer":"3471"},{"__uid":"b52cb5dc-0a62-4267-951c-cbd7364004c7","question":"A shop prices a jacket 40% above what it paid for it, then puts it on sale at 15% off that price. The jacket sells for $142.80. How many dollars did the shop pay for it?","answer":"120"},{"__uid":"fe8e278b-0762-45b1-be33-e557305a4cf6","question":"Pipe A fills a tank in 6 hours and pipe B fills it in 10 hours. Pipe C empties a full tank in 15 hours. If the tank starts empty and all three pipes are open, how many hours does it take to fill?","answer":"5"},{"__uid":"5ae9a7d7-b36f-4aac-aaaa-f8a3a44d8746","question":"How many days are there from March 3, 2024 to November 19, 2024, counting both the first and the last day?","answer":"262"},{"__uid":"122688f7-fab1-4fbb-95e5-1a6fb9f63952","question":"Sam reads 12 pages on the first day, and each day after that reads 3 more pages than the day before. On which day does Sam's running total first reach at least 400 pages?","answer":"14"},{"__uid":"4671b143-203d-417a-8d32-e4e7e6f2e50e","question":"A car gets 34 miles per gallon and gas costs $3.89 per gallon. How many dollars does the gas cost for a round trip where each way is 287 miles? Round to the nearest cent.","answer":"65.67"},{"__uid":"4b1b0b11-166d-4fe9-9866-821e426ca254","question":"If 7 workers build 3 sheds in 12 days, how many days would 4 workers take to build 5 sheds, working at the same rate?","answer":"35"},{"__uid":"940b598c-7f22-4f51-9f05-29204e4fe433","question":"What is the remainder when 3^100 + 5^50 is divided by 7?","answer":"1"}],"sel_rows":null},"position":{"x":-1200,"y":-120},"positionAbsolute":{"x":-1200,"y":-120},"dragHandle":".node-header"},{"width":312,"height":195,"id":"textfields-7333f737-ebf5-4a52-a631-5ddba1988e59","type":"textfields","data":{"title":"Reasoning effort","fields":{"f0":"off","f1":"medium"}},"position":{"x":-580,"y":-640},"positionAbsolute":{"x":-580,"y":-640