ns":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":95.83333333333334,"error":0}},"uid":"b5f33269-6cc3-4037-9a72-dd99e4b16b32","metavars":{"Expected":18,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","reasoning":"We need to find the original cost. Let cost be C. Price is 40% above: P = C * 1.4. Then sale at 15% off: Sale = P * 0.85 = 142.80. So 1.4 * 0.85 * C = 142.80 => 1.19 C = 142.80 => C = 142.80 / 1.19 = 120. So answer is 120."},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need to find the original cost. Let cost be C. Price is 40% above: P = C * 1.4. Then sale at 15% off: Sale = P * 0.85 = 142.80. So 1.4 * 0.85 * C = 142.80 => 1.19 C = 142.80 => C = 142.80 / 1.19 = 120. So answer is 120.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},{"text":12,"prompt":9,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":11},"llm":{"key":"0345fefe-6f71-4ebe-bd3c-f10956f23da0","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"d7ca51f2-afea-4ecb-9ce3-be22b2c6f43b","metavars":{"Expected":12,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"Claude Haiku 4.5","reasoning":"Let me denote the tank capacity as 1 unit.\n\nPipe A fills the tank in 6 hours, so its rate is 1/6 tank per hour.\nPipe B fills the tank in 10 hours, so its rate is 1/10 tank per hour.\nPipe C empties the tank in 15 hours, so its rate is -1/15 tank per hour (negative because it empties).\n\nWhen all three pipes are open, the combined rate is:\n1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15\n\nLet me find a common denominator. The LCM of 6, 10, and 15 is:\n6 = 2 × 3\n10 = 2 × 5\n15 = 3 × 5\nLCM = 2 × 3 × 5 = 30\n\n1/6 = 5/30\n1/10 = 3/30\n1/15 = 2/30\n\nCombined rate = 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30 = 6/30 = 1/5 tank per hour\n\nSo it takes 5 hours to fill the tank.\n\nLet me verify:\n- Pipe A in 5 hours: 5 × 1/6 = 5/6 of the tank\n- Pipe B in 5 hours: 5 × 1/10 = 5/10 = 1/2 of the tank\n- Pipe C in 5 hours: -5 × 1/15 = -5/15 = -1/3 of the tank\n\nTotal: 5/6 + 1/2 - 1/3\n\nCommon denominator is 6:\n5/6 + 3/6 - 2/6 = 6/6 = 1 ✓\n\nSo the answer is 5 hours."},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me denote the tank capacity as 1 unit.\n\nPipe A fills the tank in 6 hours, so its rate is 1/6 tank per hour.\nPipe B fills the tank in 10 hours, so its rate is 1/10 tank per hour.\nPipe C empties the tank in 15 hours, so its rate is -1/15 tank per hour (negative because it empties).\n\nWhen all three pipes are open, the combined rate is:\n1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15\n\nLet me find a common denominator. The LCM of 6, 10, and 15 is:\n6 = 2 × 3\n10 = 2 × 5\n15 = 3 × 5\nLCM = 2 × 3 × 5 = 30\n\n1/6 = 5/30\n1/10 = 3/30\n1/15 = 2/30\n\nCombined rate = 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30 = 6/30 = 1/5 tank per hour\n\nSo it takes 5 hours to fill the tank.\n\nLet me verify:\n- Pipe A in 5 hours: 5 × 1/6 = 5/6 of the tank\n- Pipe B in 5 hours: 5 × 1/10 = 5/10 = 1/2 of the tank\n- Pipe C in 5 hours: -5 × 1/15 = -5/15 = -1/3 of the tank\n\nTotal: 5/6 + 1/2 - 1/3\n\nCommon denominator is 6:\n5/6 + 3/6 - 2/6 = 6/6 = 1 ✓\n\nSo the answer is 5 hours.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}},{"text":12,"prompt":9,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":11},"llm":{"key":"ddc253f3-0e4c-4151-80a0-adc1a337810c","name":"GPT-5.4 Mini","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-mini","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"GPT-5.4 Mini","model":"openai/gpt-5.4-mini","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"cd31eefb-4b6e-4669-a02c-3f6f1844ead5","metavars":{"Expected":12,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"GPT-5.4 Mini","reasoning":"**Calculating tank fill rate**\n\nI need to compute the net rate of filling a tank. So that’s 1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15. I’ll find a common denominator, which is 30 here. That gives me 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30, resulting in 6/30. So if I simplify that, it’s 1/5 tank per hour, meaning it’ll take 5 hours to fill. My focus is just on the output, so that’s the number I’ll provide."},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"**Calculating tank fill rate**\n\nI need to compute the net rate of filling a tank. So that’s 1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15. I’ll find a common denominator, which is 30 here. That gives me 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30, resulting in 6/30. So if I simplify that, it’s 1/5 tank per hour, meaning it’ll take 5 hours to fill. My focus is just on the output, so 