he expression. Since 7 is prime, I know $3^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$ and $5^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$, which will be crucial for reducing the exponents.\n\n"},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**Exploring Modular Arithmetic**\n\nI'm applying Fermat's Little Theorem to simplify the expression. Since 7 is prime, I know $3^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$ and $5^6 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$, which will be crucial for reducing the exponents.\n\n","format":"google-gemini-v1","index":0}]}},{"text":23,"prompt":20,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":22},"llm":{"key":"234aef5b-0529-4cc3-bf54-2c4b6b76dabc","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":95.83333333333334,"error":0}},"uid":"f1c868b6-7b5d-49b8-9779-5e8e7b7e48fe","metavars":{"Expected":23,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","reasoning":"We need remainder of 3^100 + 5^50 mod 7. Compute modulo 7.\n\nFirst, 3 mod 7 = 3. Compute powers of 3 mod 7: 3^1=3, 3^2=9≡2, 3^3=2*3=6≡-1, 3^4= -1*3=-3≡4, 3^5=4*3=12≡5, 3^6=5*3=15≡1, so period 6. 100 mod 6 = 100 - 6*16=100-96=4, so 3^100 ≡ 3^4 ≡ 4 mod 7.\n\nNow 5 mod 7 = 5. Powers: 5^1=5, 5^2=25≡4, 5^3=4*5=20≡6, 5^4=6*5=30≡2, 5^5=2*5=10≡3, 5^6=3*5=15≡1, period 6. 50 mod 6 = 50 - 6*8=50-48=2, so 5^50 ≡ 5^2 ≡ 4 mod 7.\n\nSo sum: 4+4=8 ≡ 1 mod 7. Remainder is 1.\n\nFinal answer: 1"},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need remainder of 3^100 + 5^50 mod 7. Compute modulo 7.\n\nFirst, 3 mod 7 = 3. Compute powers of 3 mod 7: 3^1=3, 3^2=9≡2, 3^3=2*3=6≡-1, 3^4= -1*3=-3≡4, 3^5=4*3=12≡5, 3^6=5*3=15≡1, so period 6. 100 mod 6 = 100 - 6*16=100-96=4, so 3^100 ≡ 3^4 ≡ 4 mod 7.\n\nNow 5 mod 7 = 5. Powers: 5^1=5, 5^2=25≡4, 5^3=4*5=20≡6, 5^4=6*5=30≡2, 5^5=2*5=10≡3, 5^6=3*5=15≡1, period 6. 50 mod 6 = 50 - 6*8=50-48=2, so 5^50 ≡ 5^2 ≡ 4 mod 7.\n\nSo sum: 4+4=8 ≡ 1 mod 7. Remainder is 1.\n\nFinal answer: 1","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}]},"position":{"x":-200,"y":-300},"positionAbsolute":{"x":-200,"y":-300},"dragHandle":".node-header"},{"width":352,"height":225,"id":"evaluator-2bfc5a0e-8b81-4009-aa23-ea09f1da7690","type":"evaluator","data":{"title":"Correct?","language":"javascript","code":"// Compare the last number in the response with the table's Expected\n// column. Expected isn't in the prompt, so it rides along as a metavariable.\nfunction evaluate(response) {\n  const numbers = response.text.replace(/[$,]/g, \"\").match(/-?\\d+(\\.\\d+)?/g);\n  if (!numbers) return false;\n  const answer = parseFloat(numbers[numbers.length - 1]);\n  return Math.abs(answer - parseFloat(response.meta[\"Expected\"])) < 0.01;\n}","refresh":false,"fields":[{"text":28,"prompt":27,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":2,"question":29},"metavars":{"Expected":30,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"llm":{"key":"0345fefe-6f71-4ebe-bd3c-f10956f23da0","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-h