 + 23 = 300 + 23 = 323 minutes\n\nLet me verify my calculations:\n\nFirst leg:\n315 / 84 = ?\n315 ÷ 84 = 3.75\n0.75 × 60 = 45 minutes\nSo 3 hours 45 minutes ✓\n\nSecond leg:\n145 / 116 = ?\n145 ÷ 116 = 1.25\n0.25 × 60 = 15 minutes\nSo 1 hour 15 minutes ✓\n\nConverting everything to minutes: first leg is 225 minutes, the stop adds 23 minutes, and the second leg is 75 minutes. Adding these together gives 323 minutes total."},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me calculate this step by step.\n\nFirst leg:\n- Distance: 315 km\n- Speed: 84 km/h\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 315 / 84 = 3.75 hours = 3 hours 45 minutes\n\nStop:\n- 23 minutes\n\nSecond leg:\n- Distance: 145 km\n- Speed: 116 km/h\n- Time = Distance / Speed = 145 / 116 hours\n\nLet me calculate 145 / 116:\n145 / 116 = 1.25 hours = 1 hour 15 minutes\n\nTotal time:\n- First leg: 3 hours 45 minutes\n- Stop: 23 minutes\n- Second leg: 1 hour 15 minutes\n\nTotal = 3 hours 45 minutes + 23 minutes + 1 hour 15 minutes\n= 4 hours 60 minutes + 1 hour 23 minutes\n= 5 hours 23 minutes\n\nWait, let me recalculate:\n3 hours 45 minutes + 1 hour 15 minutes = 5 hours 0 minutes\n5 hours 0 minutes + 23 minutes = 5 hours 23 minutes\n\nSo the train arrives 5 hours and 23 minutes after 9:47 AM.\n\nThe question asks for minutes after 9:47 AM.\n5 hours 23 minutes = 5 × 60 + 23 = 300 + 23 = 323 minutes\n\nLet me verify my calculations:\n\nFirst leg:\n315 / 84 = ?\n315 ÷ 84 = 3.75\n0.75 × 60 = 45 minutes\nSo 3 hours 45 minutes ✓\n\nSecond leg:\n145 / 116 = ?\n145 ÷ 116 = 1.25\n0.25 × 60 = 15 minutes\nSo 1 hour 15 minutes ✓\n\nConverting everything to minutes: first leg is 225 minutes, the stop adds 23 minutes, and the second leg is 75 minutes. Adding these together gives 323 minutes total.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]},"llm":{"key":"0345fefe-6f71-4ebe-bd3c-f10956f23da0","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude