a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"c6b54ed2-5ae3-48a5-8a5e-ad80fe74d183"},{"text":25,"prompt":24,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":26},"metavars":{"Expected":25,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","reasoning":"We need to find area of path around rectangular garden. Garden dimensions: 23 m by 17 m. Path width 1.5 m around outside. So outer rectangle dimensions: length = 23 + 2*1.5 = 23+3 = 26 m, width = 17 + 2*1.5 = 17+3 = 20 m. Area of outer rectangle = 26*20 = 520 sq m. Area of garden = 23*17 = 391 sq m. Area of path = outer area - garden area = 520 - 391 = 129 sq m. Answer: 129."},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need to find area of path around rectangular garden. Garden dimensions: 23 m by 17 m. Path width 1.5 m around outside. So outer rectangle dimensions: length = 23 + 2*1.5 = 23+3 = 26 m, width = 17 + 2*1.5 = 17+3 = 20 m. Area of outer rectangle = 26*20 = 520 sq m. Area of garden = 23*17 = 391 sq m. Area of path = outer area - garden area = 520 - 391 = 129 sq m. Answer: 129.","format":"unknown","index":0}]},"llm":{"key":"234aef5b-0529-4cc3-bf54-2c4b6b76dabc","name":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"DeepSeek V4 Flash","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":95.83333333333334,"error":0}},"uid":"67e9b896-12a1-4550-8418-05a5b3f8967b"},{"text":16,"prompt":13,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":15},"metavars":{"Expected":16,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"Claude Haiku 4.5","reasoning":"Let me set up the problem.\n\nInitial ratio of walkers to bus takers is 5:7.\n\nSo let's say:\n- Walkers = 5k\n- Bus takers = 7k\n\nfor some constant k.\n\nAfter 6 walkers switch to taking the bus:\n- Walkers = 5k - 6\n- Bus takers = 7k + 6\n\nThe new ratio is 1:2, so:\n(5k - 6)/(7k + 6) = 1/2\n\nCross multiply:\n2(5k - 6) = 1(7k + 6)\n10k - 12 = 7k + 6\n3k = 18\nk = 6\n\nSo initially:\n- Walkers = 5(6) = 30\n- Bus takers = 7(6) = 42\n\nTotal students = 30 + 42 = 72\n\nLet me verify:\nAfter 6 walkers switch:\n- Walkers = 30 - 6 = 24\n- Bus takers = 42 + 6 = 48\n\nRatio = 24:48 = 1:2 ✓\n\nTotal students = 72"},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me set up the problem.\n\nInitial ratio of walkers to bus takers is 5:7.\n\nSo let's say:\n- Walkers = 5k\n- Bus takers = 7k\n\nfor some constant k.\n\nAfter 6 walkers switch to taking the bus:\n- Walkers = 5k - 6\n- Bus takers = 7k + 6\n\nThe new ratio is 1:2, so:\n(5k - 6)/(7k + 6) = 1/2\n\nCross multiply:\n2(5k - 6) = 1(7k + 6)\n10k - 12 = 7k + 6\n3k = 18\nk = 6\n\nSo initially:\n- Walkers = 5(6) = 30\n- Bus takers = 7(6) = 42\n\nTotal students = 30 + 42 = 72\n\nLet me verify:\nAfter 6 walkers switch:\n- Walkers = 30 - 6 = 24\n- Bus takers = 42 + 6 = 48\n\nRatio = 24:48 = 1:2 ✓\n\nTotal students = 72","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]},"llm":{"key":"0345fefe-6f71-4ebe-bd3c-f10956f23da0","name":"Claude Haiku 4.5","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"Claude Haiku 4.5","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"uid":"a027a35c-f6ab-4ac5-a025-88d9bef4e2bf"},{"text":16,"prompt":13,"fill_history":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":15},"metavars":{"Expected":16,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"GPT-5.4 Mini"},"reasoning_state":{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABqq1SAdD6z6_HSq6_481X02_v96K4l1mE2nh55jmGcYrzm7E-CFpfTw_1zxU19PUyXOZY6dtCLG2892VE6aP76PvW0k2kCb9Y8KMjA-VheP0U_rmvMG1zz1zzX5iF_psFtDP-W047B0C4YCefYh_HVsp5BQIj5nLcbjYSnHXRgxXItvqXmEP-xA18MymhlRD6WIr5eJ0sYHJeeQMP_gbrfG43NXQvZoYj6T1sA-AvqxcsrGCMUpeu9VT-ORf6n0FuDf4L8DUrE1A37jQOP2EinNCaz_L9SNQ9Bvc3rzUx8uCeu43v4c0k46ua-5G58O-tPVMR4CWNrfP1yV6HwgjGEfv66cQfrSOpJ90R9kTeWjRJgrPl0bjnP3xSQiSc8yc0WClw_oclShTuqoq2sSHyD7E9qQMErdqxr8DoBRQCjfAM6qyc9m1Y0CjdH5t2JTmF8G-B7lY-YBWf0n6KAYfNksy2uUNybwdYsZsfs6ltNkfpzxlK85aZYcR-5V9TaPoGAoevh2tJDL2lYjOXbahk5g_eMSERfhyyZzWUYo_qxsdYmiBi6OAJ3OnhkE-cyXl47JhQ_qlyhNKH9ScHqZ_ujTSj5kqya9zeNz9BAScWCyVn9kOHEY0GmmSUcHlQX1X0GtM1-KaIhisVZivI8K5H-I4GNhyMgWwc9GOCOhat5HKFC848xKcNKllUyE3lvzlf1PR2pbIUrwwHTITp2Aiq6WRSBjDUIj