lude the deposit at end of year 3? The phrase after 3 years likely after all transactions including third year's deposit? Let's examine: \"At the end of each year, after the interest is paid, she deposits another $300.\" After 3 years means at the end of year 3, after interest and deposit? Typically \"after 3 years\" includes 3 years of interest and the deposits made at the end of each of those 3 years if deposits made each year. Need compute. Let's compute including end-of-year-3 deposit: Year 1 beginning 2400; end interest 120 -> 2520; deposit 300 -> 2820. Year2 end interest 141 -> 2961; deposit 300 -> 3261. Year3 end interest 163.05 -> 3424.05; deposit 300 -> 3724.05 => $3,724. If not including end of year 3 deposit, just before deposit after interest = 3424.05 -> $3,424. Need decide.\n\nLet's parse: \"Maya puts $2,400 in an account that earns 5% interest compounded once a year. At the end of each year, after the interest is paid, she deposits another $300. How many dollars are in the account after 3 years, rounded to the nearest dollar?\" Usually if deposit at end of each year and asks after 3 years, it's after the third year's deposit? Many textbook problems: \"At the end of each year, immediately after the interest is credited, she deposits $300. How much is in account after 3 years?\" That would include the deposit at end of year 3. But phrase \"after the interest is paid, she deposits another $300\" means at the end of each year including year 3, so after 3 years account includes that deposit. However some might interpret \"after 3 years\" as after 3 full years from initial deposit, at which point the year 3 interest and the year 3 deposit have occurred, yes. So $3724.\n\nLet's ensure compound interest calculation: Compounded once a year, interest rate 5%. Each year multiply by 1.05 then add 300 at end. Formula: After 3 deposits at end years: A = P(1.05)^3 + 300[(1.05)^2 + (1.05)+1]? Wait careful: Initial P earns 3 years, deposit at end year1 earns 2 years, deposit at end year2 earns 1 year, deposit at end year3 earns 0 years. So total = 2400*(1.05)^3 + 300*(1.05)^2 + 300*(1.05) + 300. Compute: 1.05^3 = 1.157625; *2400 = 2778.30? Let's calculate: 1.157625*2400 = 2778.3 exactly? 1.157625*24=27.783, times 100=2778.3 yes. 300*1.1025=330.75; 300*1.05=315; +300 = 945.75. Sum=3724.05 => 3724. If excluding third deposit: 2400*1.157625 + 330.75 +315 = 3424.05 => 3424. The wording \"after 3 years\" plus \"at the end of each year ... deposits another $300\" includes the year 3 deposit. Answer 3724.\n\nNeed final only number.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}]},{"vars":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":26},"metavars":{"Expected":25,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"llm":"Claude Haiku 4.5","prompt":24,"responses":[25],"uid":"fe84482f-9267-42e1-b51c-25baeccb9752","reasoning":[83],"reasoning_state":[{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The garden measures 23 m by 17 m.\n\nA path 1.5 m wide runs all the way around the outside of the garden.\n\nI need to find the area of just the path.\n\nThe total area including the path would be:\n- The outer dimensions would be: (23 + 2(1.5)) by (17 + 2(1.5))\n- That's (23 + 3) by (17 + 3) = 26 by 20\n\nArea of garden plus path = 26 × 20 = 520 square meters\n\nArea of just the garden = 23 × 17 = 391 square meters\n\nArea of the path = 520 - 391 = 129 square meters\n\nLet me double-check:\n- Garden dimensions: 23 m × 17 m\n- Path width: 1.5 m on all sides\n- Outer dimensions: (23 + 1.5 + 1.5) × (17 + 1.5 + 1.5) = (23 + 3) × (17 + 3) = 26 × 20\n\nArea with path: 26 × 20 = 520 m²\nArea without path: 23 × 17 = 391 m²\nArea of path: 520 - 391 = 129 m²","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}]},{"vars":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":26},"metavars":{"Expected":25,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a 