ing_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need to find the original cost. Let cost be C. Price is 40% above: P = C * 1.4. Then sale at 15% off: Sale = P * 0.85 = 142.80. So 1.4 * 0.85 * C = 142.80 => 1.19 C = 142.80 => C = 142.80 / 1.19 = 120. So answer is 120.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}]},{"vars":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":11},"metavars":{"Expected":12,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"Claude Haiku 4.5"},"llm":"Claude Haiku 4.5","prompt":9,"responses":[12],"uid":"d7ca51f2-afea-4ecb-9ce3-be22b2c6f43b","reasoning":[82],"reasoning_state":[{"provider":"openrouter","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me denote the tank capacity as 1 unit.\n\nPipe A fills the tank in 6 hours, so its rate is 1/6 tank per hour.\nPipe B fills the tank in 10 hours, so its rate is 1/10 tank per hour.\nPipe C empties the tank in 15 hours, so its rate is -1/15 tank per hour (negative because it empties).\n\nWhen all three pipes are open, the combined rate is:\n1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15\n\nLet me find a common denominator. The LCM of 6, 10, and 15 is:\n6 = 2 × 3\n10 = 2 × 5\n15 = 3 × 5\nLCM = 2 × 3 × 5 = 30\n\n1/6 = 5/30\n1/10 = 3/30\n1/15 = 2/30\n\nCombined rate = 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30 = 6/30 = 1/5 tank per hour\n\nSo it takes 5 hours to fill the tank.\n\nLet me verify:\n- Pipe A in 5 hours: 5 × 1/6 = 5/6 of the tank\n- Pipe B in 5 hours: 5 × 1/10 = 5/10 = 1/2 of the tank\n- Pipe C in 5 hours: -5 × 1/15 = -5/15 = -1/3 of the tank\n\nTotal: 5/6 + 1/2 - 1/3\n\nCommon denominator is 6:\n5/6 + 3/6 - 2/6 = 6/6 = 1 ✓\n\nSo the answer is 5 hours.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}]},{"vars":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":11},"metavars":{"Expected":12,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"GPT-5.4 Mini"},"llm":"GPT-5.4 Mini","prompt":9,"responses":[12],"uid"