ate = 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30 = 6/30 = 1/5 tank per hour\n\nSo it takes 5 hours to fill the tank.\n\nLet me verify:\n- Pipe A in 5 hours: 5 × 1/6 = 5/6 of the tank\n- Pipe B in 5 hours: 5 × 1/10 = 5/10 = 1/2 of the tank\n- Pipe C in 5 hours: -5 × 1/15 = -5/15 = -1/3 of the tank\n\nTotal: 5/6 + 1/2 - 1/3\n\nCommon denominator is 6:\n5/6 + 3/6 - 2/6 = 6/6 = 1 ✓\n\nSo the answer is 5 hours.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}],"eval_res":{"items":[true],"dtype":"Categorical"}},{"vars":{"=reasoning_effort":66,"question":11},"metavars":{"Expected":12,"__pt":"{=reasoning_effort}Reply with only the final answer as a number, with no words, units or working.\n\n{question}","LLM_0":"GPT-5.4 Mini","reasoning":"**Calculating tank fill rate**\n\nI need to compute the net rate of filling a tank. So that’s 1/6 + 1/10 - 1/15. I’ll find a common denominator, which is 30 here. That gives me 5/30 + 3/30 - 2/30, resulting in 6/30. So if I simplify that, it’s 1/5 tank per hour, meaning it’ll take 5 hours to fill. My focus is just on the output, so that’s the number I’ll provide."},"uid":"cd31eefb-4b6e-4669-a02c-3f6f1844ead5","llm":{"key":"ddc253f3-0e4c-4151-80a0-adc1a337810c","name":"GPT-5.4 Mini","emoji":"🔀","model":"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.4-mini","base_model":"openrouter","temp":1,"formData":{"shortname":"GPT-5.4 Mini","model":"openai/gpt-5.4-mini","system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":"text","tools":"","tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":"","max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"settings":{"system_msg":"You are a helpful assistant.","temperature":1,"reasoning_effort":"off","reasoning_max_tokens":null,"response_format":{"type":"text"},"tools":[],"tool_choice":"","top_p":1,"stop":[],"max_tokens":null,"seed":null,"presence_penalty":0,"frequency_penalty":0},"progress":{"success":100,"error":0}},"prompt":9,"responses":[12],"tokens":{},"reasonin